From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alessandro Fontana <alessandro.fontana@pm.me>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 16:04:48 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] libhealthloop: Stop rearming the alarm on events

On battery, every event rearmed the slow wake alarm to a full interval,
and every event also restarts the awake poll timeout. A client calling
the HAL more often than once a minute kept both from expiring: the
battery was not read again until the driver raised an event, and the
level Android showed stayed where it was for hours.

Drop the rearm, as AOSP main does: the alarm fires at its interval
whatever the events in between.

Assisted-by: LLM
Change-Id: Ia7bc0a5495793918df2fe8677a3e703184662def
---
 health/utils/libhealthloop/HealthLoop.cpp | 9 ---------
 1 file changed, 9 deletions(-)

diff --git a/health/utils/libhealthloop/HealthLoop.cpp b/health/utils/libhealthloop/HealthLoop.cpp
index 8501f33..c603c14 100644
--- a/health/utils/libhealthloop/HealthLoop.cpp
+++ b/health/utils/libhealthloop/HealthLoop.cpp
@@ -267,15 +267,6 @@ void HealthLoop::MainLoop(void) {
             break;
         }
 
-        /*
-         * Reset slow timer to avoid excessive wakeup on interrupt
-         * It's assumed periodic_chores_interval_slow means the device being in non-charging state
-         */
-        if (nevents > 0 &&
-            wakealarm_wake_interval_ == healthd_config_.periodic_chores_interval_slow) {
-            WakeAlarmSetInterval(wakealarm_wake_interval_);
-        }
-
         for (int n = 0; n < nevents; ++n) {
             if (events[n].data.ptr) {
                 auto* event_handler = reinterpret_cast<EventHandler*>(events[n].data.ptr);
-- 
